From 6f01588e5f3f1bf5f566b17a26839d9c5554f68b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Hsieh <mike_hsieh@quantatw.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:17:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-gpu: add event log for SMA leak sensor state changes

This commit enhances the Nvidia SMA leak sensor by generating standard
OpenBMC event logs when the leak state or fault state changes.

Key changes:
- Included necessary sdbusplus event headers for Leak Detector.
- Trigger `LeakDetectedCritical` error log when the leak detector state
  or fault state transitions to `Abnormal`.
- Trigger `LeakDetectedNormal` event log when the leak detector state
  or fault state transitions back to `Normal`.

These event logs will be properly routed to Redfish Event Logs by
phosphor-logging, providing administrators with immediate notification
of critical leak detections and recovery events.

Tested:
- Verified the code compiles successfully.
- State transitions correctly generate `LeakDetectedCritical` and
  `LeakDetectedNormal` logs respectively on the BMC.
```
    {
      "@odata.id": "/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices/EventLog/Entries/283",
      "@odata.type": "#LogEntry.v1_15_0.LogEntry",
